<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n599" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ăcrōtērĭa</span></b> ,
			ōrum, n., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀκρωτήρια</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>the projecting</i> or <i>extreme part of a thing.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Of a harbor</i>, <i><span class="en">Vitr. 5,
			12</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b> In
			architecture, <i>the projecting parts of a
			pediment</i>, serving as a support for figures or statues, <i><span class="en">Vitr. 3,
				5, 12 sq.</span></i>; cf. Müll. Arch. §
		284.</div>
